before:
This example reads a label without printing the entire environment.
```javascript
const label = process.env.APP_LABEL ?? "Local app";
console.log(label);
```

Check allowed values after choosing the missing-value default.
```javascript
function readSize(env) {
  const size = env.SIZE === undefined ? "small" : env.SIZE;
  return size === "small" || size === "large" ? size : null;
}
```

after:
This example accepts a small or large size.

```javascript
function readSize(env) {
  const size = env.SIZE === undefined ? "small" : env.SIZE;
  return size === "small" || size === "large" ? size : null;
}
console.log(readSize({}));
console.log(readSize({SIZE: ""}));
```

The outputs are small and null.
